<h2 style="color: #2c3e50; border-bottom: 2px solid #3498db; padding-bottom: 6px;">1. Architecture Overview</h2>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">The new architecture consists of the following services:</p>

<table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 16px 0;">
  <tr style="background: #3498db; color: white;">
    <th style="padding: 10px; text-align: left; border: 1px solid #2980b9;">Service</th>
    <th style="padding: 10px; text-align: left; border: 1px solid #2980b9;">Stack</th>
    <th style="padding: 10px; text-align: left; border: 1px solid #2980b9;">Description</th>
  </tr>
  <tr style="background: #f8f9fa;">
    <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #dee2e6; font-weight: bold;">API Gateway</td>
    <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #dee2e6;">Go (Ocelot)</td>
    <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #dee2e6;">Entry point for all external traffic. Handles authentication, rate limiting, request routing, and API versioning.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #dee2e6; font-weight: bold;">User Service</td>
    <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #dee2e6;">Go + PostgreSQL</td>
    <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #dee2e6;">Manages user accounts, authentication, authorization, and profile data. Uses read replicas.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="background: #f8f9fa;">
    <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #dee2e6; font-weight: bold;">Product Service</td>
    <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #dee2e6;">Go + PostgreSQL + Redis</td>
    <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #dee2e6;">Product catalog, inventory management, pricing. Caches frequently accessed data in Redis.</td>
  </tr>
