<h2 style="color: #2c3e50; border-bottom: 2px solid #3498db; padding-bottom: 6px;">2. Service Boundaries</h2>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">Each service owns its data exclusively. No service may directly access another service's database. Communication happens through well-defined APIs (gRPC for internal, REST for external).</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">The bounded contexts are:</p>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li><strong>Identity &amp; Access:</strong> User Service</li>
  <li><strong>Catalog Management:</strong> Product Service</li>
  <li><strong>Transaction Processing:</strong> Order Service</li>
  <li><strong>Customer Communication:</strong> Notification Service</li>
  <li><strong>Discovery:</strong> Search Service</li>
  <li><strong>Intelligence:</strong> Analytics Service</li>
</ul>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">For domains that don't fit neatly into a single service, we use the <strong>Anti-Corruption Layer</strong> pattern (see Evans, DDD) to translate between bounded contexts.</p>

<h2 style="color: #2c3e50; border-bottom: 2px solid #3498db; padding-bottom: 6px;">3. Migration Strategy</h2>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">We will use the <strong>Strangler Fig pattern</strong>: gradually replace pieces of the monolith with microservices, routing traffic to the new services while the monolith continues to handle the rest.</p>

<h3 style="color: #2c3e50; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;">Phase 1 — Infrastructure (Weeks 1-4)</h3>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li>Set up Kubernetes cluster (we're using GKE)</li>
  <li>Deploy service mesh (Istio)</li>
  <li>Set up CI/CD pipelines with GitHub Actions</li>
  <li>Implement centralized logging (Loki + Grafana)</li>
  <li>Deploy Redis and RabbitMQ clusters</li>
</ul>

<h3 style="color: #2c3e50; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;">Phase 2 — Extract User Service (Weeks 5-8)</h3>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li>Extract authentication and user management from monolith</li>
  <li>Implement OAuth 2.0 / OpenID Connect</li>
  <li>Migrate user data with zero downtime</li>
  <li>All new sign-ups go through User Service</li>
  <li>Legacy auth still works in monolith (dual-write)</li>
</ul>

<h3 style="color: #2c3e50; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;">Phase 3 — Extract Product Service (Weeks 9-12)</h3>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li>Extract product catalog and inventory management</li>
  <li>Implement full-text search in Elasticsearch</li>
  <li>Product admin UI moved to new service</li>
  <li>Read traffic gradually shifted (20% → 50% → 100%)</li>
</ul>

<h3 style="color: #2c3e50; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;">Phase 4 — Extract Order Service (Weeks 13-18)</h3>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li>This is the most complex migration</li>
  <li>Order processing, payment, fulfillment</li>
  <li>Requires transactional outbox pattern for consistency</li>
  <li>Dual-write with verification for at least 2 weeks</li>
</ul>

<h3 style="color: #2c3e50; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;">Phase 5 — Extract Remaining Services (Weeks 19-24)</h3>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li>Notification Service</li>
  <li>Analytics Service (this can be done in parallel)</li>
  <li>Decommission monolith</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="color: #2c3e50; border-bottom: 2px solid #3498db; padding-bottom: 6px;">4. Data Management</h2>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">This is the hardest part. Here are the key decisions:</p>

<h3 style="color: #2c3e50; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;">Database per Service</h3>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">Each service gets its own database instance. No shared databases.</p>

<h3 style="color: #2c3e50; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;">Data Synchronization</h3>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">During migration, we use <strong>Change Data Capture (CDC)</strong> via Debezium to keep the monolith and new services in sync.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">We push events to Kafka topics:</p>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li><code style="background: #f4f4f4; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 3px;">user.events</code></li>
  <li><code style="background: #f4f4f4; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 3px;">product.events</code></li>
  <li><code style="background: #f4f4f4; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 3px;">order.events</code></li>
</ul>

<h3 style="color: #2c3e50; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;">Eventual Consistency</h3>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">We accept eventual consistency for cross-service queries. The API gateway handles saga orchestration where needed. For critical operations (like order placement), we use a distributed saga pattern with compensating transactions.</p>

<h3 style="color: #2c3e50; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;">CQRS</h3>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">Read models are maintained separately from write models. The Search Service maintains its own denormalized data for efficient querying.</p>

<h2 style="color: #2c3e50; border-bottom: 2px solid #3498db; padding-bottom: 6px;">5. Communication Patterns</h2>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;"><strong>Synchronous (gRPC):</strong></p>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li>Service-to-service queries</li>
  <li>Authentication/authorization checks</li>
  <li>Real-time inventory lookups</li>
</ul>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;"><strong>Asynchronous (RabbitMQ):</strong></p>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li>Event notifications</li>
  <li>Long-running task orchestration</li>
  <li>Cross-service data replication</li>
</ul>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">We use the following message patterns:</p>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li><strong>Command:</strong> Direct request to a specific service</li>
  <li><strong>Event:</strong> Broadcast to all interested services</li>
  <li><strong>Saga:</strong> Multi-step transaction with compensation</li>
</ul>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;"><strong>Retry and Circuit Breaker:</strong></p>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li>All gRPC calls use exponential backoff with jitter</li>
  <li>Circuit breaker opens after 5 failures in 30 seconds</li>
  <li>Half-open state after 15 seconds</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="color: #2c3e50; border-bottom: 2px solid #3498db; padding-bottom: 6px;">6. Observability</h2>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">Every service must expose:</p>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li><strong>Metrics:</strong> Prometheus endpoints (<code style="background: #f4f4f4; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 3px;">/metrics</code>)</li>
  <li><strong>Tracing:</strong> OpenTelemetry distributed tracing</li>
  <li><strong>Logging:</strong> Structured JSON logs to stdout</li>
</ul>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">We have three golden signals:</p>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li><strong>Latency:</strong> P50 &lt; 50ms, P95 &lt; 200ms, P99 &lt; 500ms</li>
  <li><strong>Traffic:</strong> Requests per second per endpoint</li>
  <li><strong>Errors:</strong> Error rate per status code family</li>
  <li><strong>Saturation:</strong> CPU, memory, connections per service</li>
</ul>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">Grafana dashboards are organized by service, with a top-level "Service Overview" dashboard showing key metrics for all services. Alerts are configured in AlertManager:</p>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li><span style="color: #e74c3c;">Page:</span> P99 latency &gt; 1s for 5 minutes</li>
  <li><span style="color: #e74c3c;">Page:</span> Error rate &gt; 5% for 2 minutes</li>
  <li><span style="color: #f39c12;">Warning:</span> CPU &gt; 80% for 10 minutes</li>
  <li><span style="color: #f39c12;">Warning:</span> Disk usage &gt; 85%</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="color: #2c3e50; border-bottom: 2px solid #3498db; padding-bottom: 6px;">7. Deployment</h2>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">All services are containerized and deployed to Kubernetes.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;"><strong>Deployment Strategy:</strong></p>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li>Blue-green deployment for all services</li>
  <li>Canary releases for high-risk changes (5% → 25% → 100%)</li>
  <li>Feature flags for gradual rollout</li>
</ul>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;"><strong>CI/CD Pipeline:</strong></p>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li>PR merged → Unit tests → Build image → Push to registry</li>
  <li>Deploy to staging → Integration tests → Smoke tests</li>
  <li>Deploy to production (blue-green)</li>
</ul>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;"><strong>Kubernetes Configuration:</strong></p>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li>Horizontal Pod Autoscaler based on CPU/memory</li>
  <li>Pod Disruption Budget: min 2 available</li>
  <li>Resource requests and limits for all containers</li>
  <li>Network policies to restrict inter-service traffic</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="color: #2c3e50; border-bottom: 2px solid #3498db; padding-bottom: 6px;">8. Testing Strategy</h2>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">Testing Pyramid for each service:</p>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li><strong>Unit Tests:</strong> 70% coverage minimum — Test business logic in isolation with mocked dependencies.</li>
  <li><strong>Integration Tests:</strong> 20% — Test database interactions, message queue producers/consumers.</li>
  <li><strong>Contract Tests:</strong> 5% — Use Pact for consumer-driven contract tests between services.</li>
  <li><strong>End-to-End Tests:</strong> 5% — Test critical user journeys across all services.</li>
</ul>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">We also run:</p>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li>Chaos engineering experiments (weekly)</li>
  <li>Load tests (monthly, targeting 3x peak traffic)</li>
  <li>Security scans (daily, integrated into CI)</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="color: #2c3e50; border-bottom: 2px solid #3498db; padding-bottom: 6px;">9. Rollback Plan</h2>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">Every deployment must have a corresponding rollback plan.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;"><strong>Rollback triggers:</strong></p>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li>Error rate increase &gt; 3%</li>
  <li>P99 latency increase &gt; 50%</li>
  <li>Any P0 incident opened within 30 minutes of deployment</li>
</ul>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;"><strong>Rollback procedure:</strong></p>
<ol style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li>Identify the affected service and scope</li>
  <li>If feature flagged: disable the feature flag</li>
  <li>If canary: shift traffic back to previous version</li>
  <li>If blue-green: switch active environment</li>
  <li>Monitor for 30 minutes after rollback</li>
  <li>Open incident ticket with findings</li>
</ol>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;"><strong>Database rollbacks:</strong></p>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li>All schema migrations are forward-only</li>
  <li>Additive changes only (no destructive migrations)</li>
  <li>Rollback means deploying previous application version</li>
  <li>Never roll back a database migration</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="color: #2c3e50; border-bottom: 2px solid #3498db; padding-bottom: 6px;">10. Timeline &amp; Milestones</h2>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li>Month 1-2: Foundation (Infrastructure + CI/CD)</li>
  <li>Month 3-4: User Service migration complete</li>
  <li>Month 5-6: Product Service migration complete</li>
  <li>Month 7-9: Order Service migration complete</li>
  <li>Month 10-11: Notification + Analytics migrated</li>
  <li>Month 12: Monolith decommissioned</li>
</ul>
<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;"><strong>Key milestones:</strong></p>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li><strong>M1</strong> (Week 4): Green cluster with all infra operational</li>
  <li><strong>M2</strong> (Week 8): User Service handles 100% of auth traffic</li>
  <li><strong>M3</strong> (Week 12): Product Service handles 100% of catalog</li>
  <li><strong>M4</strong> (Week 18): Order Service handles 100% of orders</li>
  <li><strong>M5</strong> (Week 24): All services migrated, monolith shutdown</li>
</ul>

